Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> writes:
> guns wrote:
> > If I make changes to the source, recompile, and then reload a previous
> > save file successfully, does that mean that the file is 100%
> > compatible with the changes, or will I discover bugs while playing?

> Depending on what parts of the source you changed; yes.

..and what exactly you do to those parts.
If you did not compile yourself the binaries that you now use, it is very
much possible that you'll end up changing some compile-time setting that
invalidates the old save files even if you don't apply any patches and
don't make any significant changes. Depending on the platform it is quite
possible that even using a C compiler different from the one the devteam
is enough to make the save file incompatible.

If you have a good game going on, it is probably a good idea to finish it
first, just to make sure.

